[quote][b]I'm working on all of these mods on my own.[/b] If you'd like to help, extend or fix one of them, co-author a new one, or join one of my bigger projects, I'm very open to it. Send me a message here on Nexus or on the [b]FarCry:Modding Discord Server[/b].[/quote]

Driving in Far Cry 2 as off-road driving: a third-person view, physics that let a car slide, lean and bounce, an engine with real gears, and new engine sounds for every car.

[b][size=4]What it adds[/size][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Third-person view[/b] - press V (rebindable under the vehicle controls) for a chase camera that swings after the car with a lag, so you see the body work on its suspension. The mouse orbits it. You see your whole body at the wheel, with the game's own driving animations. Getting out, or moving to a turret or a passenger seat, puts the first-person view back.[/*]
[*][b]Off-road physics[/b] on the car you drive - no speed limiter, weak brakes that lock the wheels into a skid, the ground's own grip so cars coast and slide, softer springs and dampers, a wider steering lock. AI drivers keep the game's physics.[/*]
[*][b]Every car tuned as the real vehicle it depicts[/b] - the Datsun 1200, Land Rover Series III, ZIL-130, Unimog 406, Jeep Wrangler, Jeep Liberty, the buggy and the quad, each carrying its weight as the real one does. The Land Rover and the big trucks ride on solid axles that twist to keep both wheels down.[/*]
[*][b]A real engine[/b] - the revs come from the gearbox: a slipping clutch as you pull away, each car's own redline with a rev limiter, gear changes as in Far Cry 3 that hold their gear up a hill. The ZIL-130 has its real five-speed gearbox, the Jeep Liberty is an automatic.[/*]
[*][b]New engine sounds for every car[/b] - recorded from real engines: idle, start and revs, with gear-change clunks on the Datsun and the big trucks, and recorded engine-off sounds.[/*]
[*][b]Quieter tyres[/b] - 10 dB down, so they no longer drown out the engine.[/*]
[*][b]Headlamps you can see[/b] - every lit headlamp shows as a bright point from afar and glares up close, on any car.[/*]
[*][b]New paints and chrome[/b] - muted paints for the Datsun, Land Rover, big truck and buggy; chrome bumpers, rims and grille on the Datsun.[/*]
[*][b]The big truck's grille[/b] with new openings, and its radiator fan spinning while the engine runs.[/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4]Tuning[/size][/b]
Every car starts at a tuning made for it in game. To change one, edit [b]bin\vehicle-overhaul.ini[/b], which holds every value for each car: engine power, top speed, shift times, brakes, steering, grip, inertia, springs and damping.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/farcry2/mods/368]FCSE[/url] 1.4.0 or later, the plugin loader this runs in. Far Cry 2 1.03, Steam or GOG.[/*]
[*]Recommended: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/farcry2/mods/388]UFCP[/url], with which headlights light the grass.[/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4]Installing[/size][/b]
The download is a JackAll layer, which both installers read as-is:
[list]
[*][b]Vortex[/b] - with the Far Cry 2 extension 0.4.0 or later, the auto-installer handles the rest.[/*]
[*][b]JackAll[/b] - 1.4.0 or later; [url=https://jbebe.github.io/farcry-sdk/jackall/installing-mods/]here's a detailed instruction[/url].[/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4]Compatibility[/size][/b]
[list]
[*][b]Mods that retune the cars[/b] keep working with it: it knows each car by the kind of vehicle it is, not by its mass or engine.[/*]
[*][b]Mods that replace car engine sounds, or the Datsun's or big truck's model[/b], change the same files; the installer reports it. Sound Overhaul is one: both replace the Datsun's idle.[/*]
[/list]
[b][size=4]Planned[/size][/b]
Shooting from the car's windows, and the game's wrecks revived as drivable vehicles.
